nate free port and/or disambiguate the container name), given mcp_free_port/mcp_managed scan running containers only.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 1: 'keep the dead live container until after a replacement is promoted (no rm -f of the serving reference)'","Plan step 3: 'start a replacement from the currently deployed MCP image on the free blue/green port'","autodeploy.sh:490 mcp_managed uses `docker ps` (running only); an exited container is not listed","autodeploy.sh:620-630 mcp_free_port derives bound ports only from mcp_managed (running)","autodeploy.sh:1151 mcp_newname=\"${MCP_CONTAINER_PREFIX}-${TARGET:0:12}-${mcp_newport}\" — same SHA + same port => identical name as the retained exited backend"],"finding":"The self-heal replacement can collide with the retained dead container's name/port: mcp_managed()/mcp_free_port() scan RUNNING containers only, so the exited dead-live backend is invisible to the free-port pick, and starting a replacement 'from the currently deployed MCP image' (same SHA => same ${PREFIX}-${TARGET:0:12}-${port} name) can produce a docker-run name collision with the retained exited container.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5ff0691d0420dc21","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA / design decision (2026-09-07), steps 1 & 3","norm_id":"ndbaf21985385ad78","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["OOM-killed live backend on port A stays exited; self-heal reuses the currently-deployed SHA and mcp_free_port returns A (exited container not seen as bound); docker run --name collides and the heal aborts, leaving /mcp still 502."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that self-heal must pick the blue/green port NOT equal to the dead live container's port, and derive a replacement container name that cannot equal the retained exited container's name (e.g. add a heal-attempt suffix) when the deployed SHA is unchanged.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a live-verification step that kills/OOMs the live MCP container with NO source change pending, then confirms autodeploy self-heals and /mcp recovers (emitting AUTODEPLOY_MCP_SELF_HEAL), rather than verifying via a scratch-change redeploy.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design fires the self-heal 'on every tick before ordinary source-change deploy decisions' and specifically when there is 'no source change pending'","Live step: 'confirm no persistent 502 after intentionally abandoning scratch test changes' — abandoning scratch changes triggers a source-change redeploy, which is the pre-existing cutover path, not the self-heal branch"],"finding":"The live-verification step exercises the source-change redeploy path, not the new no-source-change self-heal path the ticket fixes.","group_criteria":nu