,"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'RED test ... asserts the tick starts a replacement, flips upstream ... and only then reaps the dead backend'; 'Companion test covers low-memory self-heal refusal'","No test named for a replacement that starts but fails the readiness/nginx gate — the failure path of the new flow."],"finding":"The testing plan has a RED success test and a low-memory-refusal test, but names no test for the self-heal failure path where the started replacement fails a readiness gate (/health, nginx-test) — the exact arm whose mishandling reproduces the persistent 502.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbac1e343b7777565","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / verification plan","norm_id":"n683a8ec76bf87dc8","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition contract for a failed self-heal attempt: whether it is retryable (next tick re-attempts, dead backend kept, /mcp still 502 only transiently) vs a bounded skip, so a gate-failing replacement does not leave /mcp permanently pinned to the dead backend.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.23,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'require the same /health readiness ... gates as a normal MCP cutover'; 'emit ... existing error markers on failure'","No disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal) is stated for the case where the replacement fails a gate; the plan states markers but not what /mcp surfaces or whether the next tick retries."],"finding":"The gate opens (a self-heal/failover arm is added), and the plan states the low-memory-refusal disposition and failure markers, but it does not state the disposition surfaced when the self-heal itself fails a readiness gate (/health, store-readiness, nginx-test) — i.e. whether /mcp stays 502 or the heal is retryable on the next tick, which is exactly the persistent-502 recurrence this ticket must prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f649f1eecc1f33981","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA step 4 — '/health readiness, store-readiness, startup-handshake, nginx-test, and nginx-reload gates'","norm_id":"n77426df58da3e374","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Declare that a replacement that fails any readiness gate leaves the dead backend in place and the heal retryable on the next tick (transient), and that the low-memory refusal is a bounded skip retried when memory frees — never a terminal state that pins /mcp to 502.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na"