on of the whole heal sequence is not stated (check-then-act on 'live container not running' then start replacement is a TOCTOU window)."],"finding":"The self-heal mutates shared blue/green port-pool + nginx-upstream state, but the plan does not state concurrency ownership: whether two ticks can overlap, or how a self-heal tick interacts with a concurrent source-change deploy competing for the same free port / upstream pointer.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f13aa3d45d2c7c1ee","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA step 3-5 — 'start a replacement ... on the free blue/green port' / 'atomically flip nginx'","norm_id":"n139f7f9c949ecb85","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two overlapping ticks (or a heal tick plus a source-change deploy) both observe the dead live backend and both claim the single free port, leaving the pool exhausted or nginx flipped to a half-started backend."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the self-heal behavior on the unreadable-MemAvailable (-1) branch (fail-open as today, or refuse), and note whether a single dead backend + one replacement stays within the 2-port/2x-overlap memory envelope.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'honor the existing MCP memory floor and two-port cap so healing cannot worsen the same memory-pressure class'","autodeploy.sh:1137-1142: `[ \"$mcp_mem\" -ge 0 ] && [ \"$mcp_mem\" -lt MCP_MEM_MIN_MB ]` aborts, but `mcp_mem < 0` (unreadable) logs and proceeds fail-OPEN","Companion test as described covers only the readable-below-floor refusal, not the -1 fail-open branch"],"finding":"The plan requires honoring the existing memory floor but does not state the intended self-heal behavior on the unreadable-MemAvailable (-1) branch, which the current deploy path treats as fail-OPEN — in an OOM-triggered heal, failing open can restart straight back into the OOM class the plan says it must not worsen.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc35a391964c6a33c","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA step 2 and Testing/verification plan (low-memory companion test)","norm_id":"na92798bf1f0ffae1","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Box under OOM pressure where /proc/meminfo read fails or is stubbed unreadable; self-heal proceeds with a 2x overlap start and re-triggers OOM."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_